From 8f39b133ed0cf13fb83883dd8a3417c358c38f99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 10:21:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dicts: translate the Service Intercept + pending-banner
 tokens into all 24 languages

RFW_258-275 (18 tokens) went in as English placeholders across the lockstep;
this replaces them with real translations in the 24 non-EN dicts, matching how
RBKP_1-18 and the rest of the RFW_ range are already carried.

Covers the Service Intercept card (title, the explanatory lede, Mode / From /
Intercept port / Server / Server port / Exempt / Return path and their option
words) and the page-level pending banner added alongside it - including the two
long notes, which are the ones that actually have to be understood: that the
target is always exempt from its own rule, and that Return path on Auto only
adds address translation when the server shares a network with the clients.

Lockstep holds at 6768 lines x 25 dicts. reaper_langcheck 0 breakers over 22
pages - worth checking here rather than assuming, since several of these
translations contain apostrophes that would break a single-quoted JS context;
ours sit in backticks and HTML, so they are safe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
